  "description": "Vitus E-Escarpe VRS: The right bike for any job\n\nThe E-Escarpe is an all-mountain eMTB designed for singletrack, after work laps, and for those looking for a pedal-assist alternative to a standard trail bike. Its balanced geometry is a blast uphill and down, and its Shimano EP801 drive system is intuitive and can be tuned to suit the way you ride.\n\nIt’s an eMTB for the rider who wants a nimble and responsive e-bike; a bike that’s a little less of an e-enduro brawler and instead a little more versatile and responsive.\n\nClosely based on our award-winning Escarpe trail bike, the E-Escarpe is powered by the grunty and Shimano STEPS EP801 drive unit and a 630Wh battery. This motor system makes 85Nm of climb-eating torque and peaks at 600w of power — a capable tool in an all-mountain setting.\n\nOur goal was to make an eMTB that handled exactly like the rock-solid Escarpe trail bike, which is exactly where our designers landed. We began development on the E-Escarpe by starting with the original Escarpe frame and making small tweaks to make room for the EP801 drive system and adjusted the geometry for eMTB use. The result is an e-bike chassis that’s efficient on climbs and an absolute blast on descents; flickable enough to rail switchbacks and blitz rock gardens while still placing emphasis on uphill efficiency. It’s what we at Vitus envision as the ideal all-day, do-anything, ride-anywhere eMTB.\n\nThe E-Escarpe VRS is built around Shimano’s SLX 12-speed drivetrain and a set of SRAM DB8 4-piston hydraulic brakes. The suspension is a 150mm RockShox Lyric Select fork paired with a RockShox Super Deluxe Select R shock with 140mm of travel in the rear. The rest of the kit is finished with Nukeproof components.\n\nBuilt for variable terrain, after-work power laps, and undulating days in the saddle, the E-Escarpe is the perfect tool for any job.\n\nRockShox Lyrik Select & Super Deluxe Select R suspension\n\nEfficient Shimano STEPS EP801 motor with 630Wh internal battery\n\nShimano SLX 1x12 speed drivetrain\n\nPowerful SRAM DB8 4 piston hydraulic disc brakes\n\nNukeproof Neutron V2 tubeless ready wheelset with tape applied\n\nConfidence inspiring Maxxis Assegai & Minion DHR II tyres",
